To fix this we keep the same functional layout but use the generic symbol name and supply the proper value string (`XC6206P332MR`, `XC6206P100MR`, `XC6206P25MR`) in the `value` field.  The `reference` fields are unique identifiers that will be used for connections and for the global labels that are added later.

Below is a concise explanation of the key decisions made in the corrected script.

| Section | Reasoning |
|---------|-----------|
| **Center symbol** | The charge‑pump is placed at the centre of the page (`center_x_1=150`, `center_y_1=110`) so that all other components can be positioned relative to it.  No rotation or mirroring is needed because the symbol is symmetric. |
| **XC6206 regulators** | Three regulators are placed to the left of the charge‑pump: C1 (3.3 V LDO), C2 (3 V LDO), and C3 (1 V LDO).  All are the same generic symbol “XC6206PxxxMR”; the `value` field carries the exact part number.  Rotation is 0° to keep the pins in the standard orientation. |
| **Flying capacitors** | Two 1 nF capacitors (C4, C5) are placed around the fly‑switch node.  They are the negative and positive sides of the charge‑pump’s internal fly‑switch.  Their positions are offset vertically to avoid overlap. |
| **Output capacitor** | C6 (1 µF) is placed on the right side of the charge‑pump to provide the negative output.  It is connected to the VIN pin of the charge‑pump (the output pin of the regulator). |
| **Power symbols** | Three +1.8 V symbols are added to represent the power rails that feed the charge‑pump and the LDOs.  Ground symbols are added at the bottom of each path. |
| **Labels** | Global labels (`VIN_NEG`, `VBUS_NEG`, `V_BUSB`, `V_OUT`) are placed next to the corresponding pins of the LDOs so that the schematic can be connected to the rest of the design.  The `text_orient` is chosen to keep the label text readable relative to the pin. |
| **Connections** | 1. **Ground chain** – GND pins of C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6 are all tied together.  2. **Charge‑pump** – `VIN` of C1 → `VIN` of the charge‑pump; `VOUT` of the charge‑pump → `VI` of C1 (the VIN pin of C1).  3. **Fly‑switch** – `OUT` of C4 and `OUT` of C5 are tied together; their connection to the `AO` pin of the charge‑pump creates the inverting action.  4. **Load** – The negative output is taken from `VOUT` of C6 and is connected to the rest of the circuit via the label.  5. **LDOs** – `VI` pins are fed from the charge‑pump output and the `VO` pins are connected to the load and the negative output. |
